<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="057" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>ADR-038 Amendment A2 — `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/**` is the ninth KEEP path</title>
    <phase>4 Parity, deploy, close</phase>
    <gate>startable — owner authorised the amendment 2026-09-19 (CLAUDE.md §6.5 Path B)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <!-- Task 079, 2026-10-02: status was 'not-started' while the index read done. Synced to completed: CLOSED FOR THIS PROJECT, not executed here. Handed to unified-access-control-r2 (GitHub #1014) by owner decision 2026-09-28. -->
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Edits `.claude/` directive surface (main-session-only per CLAUDE.md §3) and amends a binding ADR. The failure mode is silent: an amendment that updates some copies of the KEEP-path list and not others leaves `/test-diet` recommending deletion of protected tests — which is exactly what A1 did and what this task must repair.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>ADR amendment authoring — the reasoning (why the category deserves protection, what the amendment does NOT grant) is the deliverable, not the edit.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>`.claude/skills/**` and `.claude/constraints/**` are hot-path (serial PRs only) and sub-agents cannot write to `.claude/` at all.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>skill-directive, testing, adr, documentation</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Amend ADR-038 to add `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/**` as the NINTH KEEP path category, and repair the two copies of the KEEP-path list that Amendment A1 left stale.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer amending a binding ADR. The deliverable is the reasoning — why this category deserves protection and what the amendment does not grant — not the mechanical edit.</role>

  <goal>`/test-diet` stops classifying the repo's largest test project as a path violation, and every copy of the KEEP-path list says the same thing.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Found 2026-09-19 by `/test-diet` at this project's pre-wrap-up pass. This project added **71 test
      methods across 8 files** under `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/**`, which is not among ADR-038's eight
      KEEP paths. `constraints/testing.md` says a test MUST NOT be introduced outside them — so taken
      literally, every one is a violation and `/test-diet` heuristic 1 recommends `git mv` or deletion.

      That reading is wrong, and the same wrongness has occurred twice before. The `Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests`
      project holds roughly **12,400 tests** — the repo's largest suite. A classifier that flags it wholesale
      is describing a target state the codebase does not occupy. This is the identical shape as Amendment A1
      (2026-08-24), which added `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/**` after `/test-diet` classified every architecture
      test as a delete candidate — *"recommended deleting the mechanism the ADR requires"* — and as the
      2026-07-09 `tests/integration/seam/**` drift.

      Owner decision 2026-09-19: **Path B — amend the ADR** (CLAUDE.md §6.5).
    </background>

    <notes>
      **A1 IS THE TEMPLATE.** `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md:543-600` carries Amendment A1's shape:
      a dated section header, a "what it said before" table, the new MUST rule, and an explicit "what this
      does NOT grant" scope limit. A2 mirrors it.

      **THE BLAST RADIUS IS SIX FILES, AND TWO ARE ALREADY STALE.** Measured 2026-09-19 — these enumerate the
      KEEP paths:

      | File | State after A1 |
      |---|---|
      | `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md` | current |
      | `.claude/constraints/testing.md` | current |
      | `.claude/skills/test-diet/SKILL.md` | current |
      | `tests/CLAUDE.md` | current |
      | `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` | **STALE — still says "6 KEEP path categories"; missing `seam` AND `ArchTests`** |
      | `docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md` | **STALE — does not mention `Spaarke.ArchTests`** |

      Note there is **no concise `.claude/adr/ADR-038-*.md`** — the concise form is the single row at
      `.claude/adr/INDEX.md:60`. A2 must fix that row's count AND its list, not just append to it.

      **THE POINT OF THIS TASK IS THAT PARTIAL UPDATES ARE THE FAILURE MODE.** A1 updated four of six copies.
      The two it missed are why this list has been wrong for a month. Update all six or the amendment has not
      landed.

      🛑 **BLOCKED 2026-09-28 — AMENDMENT-NUMBER COLLISION. Do not execute this task as written.**

      Found at Step 0.5's mandatory hot-path `/conflict-check`, before any edit.

      **`unified-access-control-r2` has ALREADY authored an "Amendment A2" to ADR-038** — a different
      amendment on a different subject, dated **2026-09-18**, owner-ratified, raised by their task 106
      Step 9.5: *"ban B8 targets reflection into privates, not `InternalsVisibleTo`"*. It lives on
      `work/unified-access-control-r2` in **open PR #950** and is **not on master** (master's ADR-038 carries
      **A1 only**). Their `.claude/constraints/testing.md` ban #8 already cites *"ADR-038 **Amendment A2**,
      2026-09-18"* by number.

      Consequences, all of which change this task's contract:

      1. **This amendment must be A3, not A2** — the title, the goal element and six criterion entries say A2.
         Two different A2 sections in one ADR would make every *"ADR-038 Amendment A2"* citation ambiguous.
      2. **Three of the six files are in PR #950** — `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md`,
         `.claude/constraints/testing.md`, `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`. `.claude/**` is declared **serial PRs
         only**; `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` is also in draft PR #935 (`code-quality-and-assurance-r4`), so three
         projects contend on that one file. PR #950 is **CONFLICTING**, +64,820/-8,041, last updated
         2026-09-28 — not merging cleanly or imminently.
      3. **Their A2 NARROWED ban B8.** This task's constraint *"do not weaken any existing ban; B1-B17 continue
         to apply in full"* must therefore be read against **their amended B8**, not master's. Authoring from
         master's text would silently revert an owner-ratified amendment.

      **Splitting the work by contention is FORBIDDEN**, and specifically by this task: doing the three
      uncontested files (`.claude/skills/test-diet/SKILL.md`, `docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md`,
      `tests/CLAUDE.md`) and deferring the rest **is** the partial-update failure mode 057 exists to repair —
      it would reproduce A1's error at larger scale.

      **The underlying finding is unaffected and still valid**: the KEEP-path list is still eight and still
      excludes `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/**`, and `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` still says *"6 KEEP path
      categories"* even on UAC-r2's branch. Only the numbering and the sequencing are blocked.

      Awaiting an owner decision between: (1) renumber to A3 and execute after #950 merges; (2) execute now as
      A3 against #950's branch content; (3) hand the amendment to `unified-access-control-r2`, who already own
      ADR-038 amendments and are already editing all three contested files.
    </notes>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §3">`.claude/**` edits are MAIN-SESSION-ONLY. Do not dispatch this to a sub-agent — it will fail with "Edit denied", which is the boundary working correctly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6.5">This is a Path B amendment. It MUST state what it does NOT grant, mirroring A1's scope limit — protection is not exemption from review.</constraint>
    <constraint source="A1 precedent">Do NOT weaken any existing ban. B1-B17 continue to apply to the new category in full; this amendment changes WHERE a test may live, never WHAT it may do.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">Do NOT move or delete any existing test. The amendment legitimises the location; it does not license churn.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>`docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md` carries a new "Amendment A2" section mirroring A1's structure (dated header, what-it-said-before, new MUST rule, explicit non-grants).</criterion>
    <criterion>The §2 KEEP-path table in that ADR gains a ninth row for `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/**`, with a category name and a description of what legitimately lives there (BFF service/filter/infrastructure tests that are neither pure domain logic nor integration).</criterion>
    <criterion>The ADR's "Encode N KEEP path categories" line reads **9**, not 8.</criterion>
    <criterion>`.claude/constraints/testing.md` §1 table gains the ninth row and its heading count is corrected.</criterion>
    <criterion>`.claude/skills/test-diet/SKILL.md` heuristic 1 path list includes the new path — this is the line that actually drives the classifier.</criterion>
    <criterion>`tests/CLAUDE.md` KEEP-path list gains the row.</criterion>
    <criterion>`.claude/adr/INDEX.md:60` is REPAIRED: count corrected to 9 and the list updated to include `seam`, `Spaarke.ArchTests` AND the new path. Its two-amendment staleness is fixed, not merely appended to.</criterion>
    <criterion>`docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md` is REPAIRED the same way — it is missing `ArchTests` from A1 as well as the new path.</criterion>
    <criterion>A grep for `tests/unit/domain` across `.claude/`, `docs/`, `tests/` returns no file whose KEEP-path list disagrees with any other. State the command and its output in the task note.</criterion>
    <criterion>The amendment explicitly states it does NOT exempt the category from B1-B17, from code-review, or from the same-PR-replacement rule on deletion.</criterion>
    <criterion>No test file is added, moved, or deleted by this task.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a seventh file enumerating the KEEP paths is discovered that this task's list does not name, STOP and report it before editing — an incomplete list is the defect being fixed, and silently extending the scope mid-task reproduces A1's error.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md:543-600` (Amendment A1) and adopt its structure.</step>
    <step>Write Amendment A2, including the non-grants section.</step>
    <step>Update the ADR's §2 table and its "Encode N categories" line.</step>
    <step>Update the four current copies; REPAIR the two stale ones (`.claude/adr/INDEX.md`, `docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md`) including their A1 gaps.</step>
    <step>Re-grep to prove all six now agree; record the command and output.</step>
    <step>Write `notes/057-adr038-amendment-a2.md` recording the finding, the owner decision, and the six-file reconciliation.</step>
  </steps>

